WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.512
Question nineteen. Highlight: uncompressed mono; one thousand twenty-four by seven hundred sixty-eight; one bit per pixel; one K B = one thousand twenty-four bytes.

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:18.157
Useful: total bits ÷ eight → bytes, then ÷ one thousand twenty-four → K B.

00:00:18.157 --> 00:00:21.743
Useless: mono story colour — formula unchanged.

00:00:21.743 --> 00:00:26.931
Option A. Seven hundred sixty-eight K B: often missed ÷ eight — cut.

00:00:26.931 --> 00:00:32.576
Option B. One thousand twenty-four K B: mistaking one side for size — cut.

00:00:32.576 --> 00:00:37.611
Option C. One hundred ninety-two K B: common mid-step error — cut.

00:00:37.611 --> 00:00:40.053
Option D. Ninety-six K B — keep.

00:00:40.053 --> 00:00:49.894
One thousand twenty-four times seven hundred sixty-eight, divided by eight, divided by one thousand twenty-four ≈ ninety-six K B.

00:00:49.894 --> 00:00:52.488
Therefore the correct answer is D.
